/* Notes on the selector forms used in this sheet (0.0.4). It is adopted by every wz-* shadow root, so what
   matters here is how much work one rule costs per component. None of these forms changes what a rule
   matches or which rule wins.

   1. "@media all { ... }" blocks are state gates: every selector inside starts with the same
      ":host-context(html[data-wme-studio...="..."]...)" and the script switches the block off while that
      state is not active. Where :host-context() is supported, the script also drops that prefix from the
      rules of a gate when the sheet is first used (the gate already guarantees it) and gives its specificity
      back with ":not(.ws-0)...:not(ws-0)", the same way the universal rules were handled before.

   2. "S:is(A B > *)" is "A B > S" with the ancestors written on the subject. A leading ":host(...)" or
      ":host-context(...)" stays in front. The browser keeps one invalidation entry per ancestor name and per
      shadow root; written this way the ancestors do not create those entries.

   3. ":where(X):is(X, Y, ...)", one list member per alternative, is ":is(X, Y, ...)" spelled so that each
      member can be filed under X. */

